the V6 transports park a cooperative task on a socket through host_wait_readable, whose Windows arm is not there yet: the async I/O reactor has its epoll backend and the IOCP / WSAPoll backend is the roadmapped follow-on (docs/plans/2026-09-11-async-io-reactor.md item 4); under wine a parked socket read reports EOF (testsocketpark: task-eof), so every listen:// seat, the ws framer, the attach relay and discovery are out of the win64 domain until that slice lands
